 ## Overview
-This method implements the rendering phase of Gaussian Avatar Reconstruction by leveraging the Unity Sentis framework to execute Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) as custom compute shaders on the GPU [S1]. It solves the problem of dynamically predicting 3D Gaussian attributes (position, scale, rotation, opacity, and spherical harmonics) from static anchor features and a time-varying context encoding $\Psi(x)$ without CPU-GPU synchronization bottlenecks [S1]. Unlike static splatting, this approach allows for real-time appearance changes by invoking the MLP with different encodings, while maintaining a fixed memory footprint since the number of predicted Gaussians remains constant [S1].
